<Layout
	title="About"
	description="The Tredyffrin Easttown Historical Society collects local history for Tredyffrin and Easttown townships in Chester County, Pennsylvania."
>
	<p class="font-sans text-sm tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-on-surface-variant">About</p>
	<h1 class="mt-3 text-display-sm">Tredyffrin Easttown Historical Society</h1>
	<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl font-sans text-on-surface">
		Founded in 1936, the Society is the oldest community organization on the Upper Main Line
		conducting local historical research and collecting local resources and photographs for the
		townships of Tredyffrin and Easttown in eastern Chester County, Pennsylvania.
	</p>
	<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl font-sans text-on-surface-variant">
		This site publishes the History Quarterly digital archives, the image collection, the document
		collection, and township research. Membership, events, and the store remain on
		<a href="https://www.tehistory.org" class="text-primary">tehistory.org</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
